munities clarify their career direction and to increase their competitiveness and connections. This list continues to grow as we discover more. Career Services Contact Student Success Center Noel Memorial Library 318-797-5062 career@lsus.edu Instagram Facebook YouTube Student/Alum Career Resources Affinity Group Resources LSUS Handshake login Micro-Internships at LSUS Hire Pilots African American/Black Students and Alumni Job Websites: Diversity Employers Black Career Network African-American Hires Black Career Women’s Network Congressional Black Caucus Inroads Internship Program Publications: Equal Opportunity Publications Black Entrepreneur Magazine Professional Organizations: Black Enterprise ColorComm: Business Community for Women of Color in the Communications Industry National Association of Negro Business and Professional Women’s Clubs, Inc. National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP) National Association of Black Accountants, Inc. (NABA) National Association of Black Owned Broadcasters National Black Law Students Association (NBLSA) National Association of Black Journalists (NABJ) National Black MBA Association, Inc. (NBMBAA) National Black Nurses Association, Inc. (NBNA) National Society of Black Engineers (NSBE) Organization of Black Designers The Association of Black Psychologists United Negro College Fund American Indian/Indigenous Students and Alumni Job Websites: Indian Health Service: The Federal Health Program for American Indians and Alaska Natives Inroads Internships National Congress of American Indians Native American Jobs and Career Resources Native Hire RBC Publications: Infotracer United States Tribes Tribal College: Journal of American Indian Higher Education Professional Organizations: American Indian Science and Engineering Society Association for American Indian Physicians Federally Recognized Indian Tribes and Resources for Native Americans WorkforeGPS | Job Training & Employment Services for Native American Communi