ey Act Financial Aid Summer Form Satisfactory Academic Progress Policy Title IV Refund Policy Financial Aid Staff Code of Conduct Eligibility and Conditions Tuition Insurance Higher Education Emergency Relief Fund (HEERF) Student Life Academic Success Athletics Bookstore Career Services Student/Alum Career Resources Affinity Group Resources Handshake Micro-Internships at LSUS Hire Pilots Community Standards Transparency Reporting Counseling Services Cares What We Offer Resource Guide Disability Support Events Food Pantry Food Services STACKS Coffee Shop The Port Grille LSUS Catering Housing Living in Shreveport Pilot Dining Dollars Student Activities and Organizations Student Success Center First Year Experience First Generation Programs Student Success Initiatives Life After LSUS LSUS Alumni Association Career Services Community Office of Community Engagement Center for Business & Econ. Research CBER Reports NWLA Economic Dashboard Data Visualizations Center for NWLA Regional Impact Events Management Hire Pilots Human Performance Nexus Research & Teaching Strength Sports Community Service Institutional Effectiveness & Planning Institute for Nonprofit Administration & Research Professional Development @ INAR INAR Research & Consulting Marketing and Communications Brand Guidelines Pioneer Heritage Center RRWMI About the Red River W Basin RRWMI Research Projects Spring Street Museum Strategy Alternatives Consortium Triad Speakers Home Student Life Career Services Micro-Internships at LSUS Micro-Internships at LSUS HELM: Hands-on Experience & Learning with Micro-Internships In January 2026, LSUS is working with Parker Dewey to launch a program that will connect students and employers in a new way: HELM, or Hands-on Experience & Learning with Micro-Internships. HELM provides students with short-term, paid, professional assignments that are like those given to new hires or interns. These projects will allow students to demonstrate skills, explore career paths, and build networks as they seek the right full-time role. HELM enables employers to building lasting relationships with students at LSU Shreveport and: Deepen assessment of the candidate’s skills without revamping their entire hiring process Differentiate their employer brand to gain a competitive advantage in hiring Build and sustain a pipeline of early-career talent Keep high-potential candidates warm as they complete their degree Connect with students early in their academic careers HELM Student Information To be eligible to participate in HELM, you must: Be an undergraduate student Have completed 15 credits or more Students can apply for a Micro-Internship project through the LSUS HELM Student Portal . Applications will open the first week of March, with projects to begin in May 2026. Register for the Student Micro-Internships Info Session on Thursday, February 19 at 1 p.m. CST. This info session will allow students to hear an overview of what Micro-Internships are and their value, view examples of projects, and see a brief demonstration of the platform. Can’t make it to the info session? Register anyway and receive a recording and the slides after the student info session has concluded. HELM Employer Information Employers interested in participating in the HELM program must develop projects for LSUS students to complete within 15 or 30 hours, receiving coaching from Parker Dewey along the way. Projects must be posted by the first week of March so that students can begin their projects starting in May 2026. Employers can post their micro-internship projects through the LSUS HELM Employer Portal . Watch our Employer Micro-Internships Info Session . Learn how Micro-Internships can connect you with LSUS students more effectively, on-demand, and without adding to your workload, all at no cost to you. Career Services Contact Student Success Center Noel Memorial Library 318-797-5062 career@lsus.edu Instagram Facebook YouTube Student/Alum Career Resources Affinity Group Resources LSUS Handshake login Micro-Internships at LSUS Hire Pilots Anchor In at LSUS You have the potential. We have the community, resources, and affordable education you need to achieve your purpose. Apply Today Request Info Visit LSUS One University Place Shreveport, LA 71115 (800) 229-5957 (318) 797-5000 About LSUS Campus Map News Events Media and Public Record Requests Employment Opportunities Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Admissions First Time Freshmen International Graduate Admissions Military and Veterans Costs and Aid Quick Links LSUS Police Privacy Policy Accessibility Notice of Non-Discrimination Clery Report Copyright © 2026. Louisiana State University Shreveport. All Rights Reserved.\nLSUS is an Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer."
